    <body>
      <chapter eId="chapter-2">
        <num>2</num>
        <heading>Adducing evidence</heading>
        <content>
          <p>		<i>INTRODUCTORY NOTE</i></p>
          <p>		<i>Outline of this Chapter </i></p>
          <p>This Chapter is about ways in which evidence is adduced.</p>
          <p><ref href="#part-2">Part&#160;2</ref>.1 is about adducing evidence from witnesses.</p>
          <p><ref href="#part-2">Part&#160;2</ref>.2 is about adducing documentary evidence.</p>
        </content>
        <part eId="chapter-2__part-2.1">
          <num>2.1</num>
          <heading>Witnesses</heading>
          <division eId="chapter-2__part-2.1__dvs-1">
            <num>1</num>
            <heading>Competence and compellability of witnesses</heading>
            <section eId="chapter-2__part-2.1__dvs-1__sec-12">
              <num>12</num>
              <heading>Competence and compellability</heading>
              <content>
                <p>Except as otherwise provided by this Act:</p>
              </content>
              <paragraph eId="chapter-2__part-2.1__dvs-1__sec-12__para-a">
                <num>a</num>
                <content>
                  <p>every person is competent to give evidence; and</p>
                </content>
              </paragraph>
              <paragraph eId="chapter-2__part-2.1__dvs-1__sec-12__para-b">
                <num>b</num>
                <content>
                  <p>a person who is competent to give evidence about a fact is compellable to give that evidence.</p>
                </content>
              </paragraph>
            </section>
          </division>
        </part>
        <part eId="chapter-2__part-2.2">
          <num>2.2</num>
          <heading>Documents</heading>
          <section eId="chapter-2__part-2.2__sec-51">
            <num>51</num>
            <heading>Original document rule abolished</heading>
            <content>
              <p>The principles and rules of the common law that relate to the means of proving the contents of documents are abolished.</p>
            </content>
            <authorialNote placement="end" eId="note-17" marker="17">
              <content>
                <p>Note:	Section&#160;182 gives the provisions of this Part a wider application in relation to Commonwealth records and certain Commonwealth documents.</p>
              </content>
            </authorialNote>
          </section>
        </part>
      </chapter>
